<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="YuneBridge" pubkey="" timestamp="1792913634" url="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/quompacc/yunebridge/fdroid/repo" version="20002"><description>Official repository of YuneBridge, a Gadgetbridge fork with a redesigned interface. Source code: https://github.com/quompacc/yunebridge</description></repo><application id="io.github.quompacc.yunebridge"><id>io.github.quompacc.yunebridge</id><added>2026-10-25</added><lastupdated>2026-10-25</lastupdated><name>YuneBridge</name><summary>Gadgetbridge fork with a redesigned interface – no cloud, no vendor account</summary><desc>YuneBridge is a fork of &lt;a href=&quot;https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge&quot;&gt;Gadgetbridge&lt;/a&gt; with a redesigned, modern interface. It talks to your smartwatch, fitness band or earbuds directly – without the vendor's app, without a cloud and without an account.

All functions of Gadgetbridge are kept, including:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Activity, sleep, heart rate and other health data, stored only on your phone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notifications, calls and music control on the watch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Installing watch faces, apps and firmware files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alarms, weather and many device-specific settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data export and backup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

YuneBridge can be installed next to Gadgetbridge. Device support, protocols and background services come unchanged from Gadgetbridge; YuneBridge only changes the look.

YuneBridge is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later. All credit for device support goes to the Gadgetbridge developers and contributors.
